{"seconds": 98.0, "exit": 0, "final": "After **Rg2+ Kf5**, I have **Rg5+** forcing **Kxg5**, which loses my rook. So that's not the right continuation. But Black won't play **Kf5** because it's worse than the other options. The key is that after **Kh6** or **Kh4**, the rook is hanging and I take it.\n\nLet me also verify one more time that this is the best move by checking if there's anything better than **Rg2+**. Looking back at the legal moves, the main candidates were **Rxh5+** and **Rg2+**. I've now seen that **Rg2+** wins material decisively. **Rxh5+** only wins a pawn and my rook becomes vulnerable. So **Rg2+** is clearly better.\n\n**Coaching note**: \"When your opponent's piece is defended only by the king, look for a check that drives the king away. Here, Rg2+ forces Black's king from g5, and the rook on f4 suddenly hangs. This is called deflection\u2014using a forcing move (check) to remove the defender of another piece.\"\n\nBest move: **Rg2+**\nMain line: **Rg2+ Kh6 Kxf4** (winning Black's rook) or if **Rg2+ Rg4 Rxg4+ Kxg4/hxg4** (also winning material)\n\nMotif: **attraction** (the check attracts/deflects the king away from defending the rook)\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Rg2+\", \"line\": [\"Rg2+\", \"Kh6\", \"Kxf4\"], \"motifs\": [\"attraction\", \"deflection\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kp/5r2/4K3/P6R/8 w - - 15 57"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kp/5r2/4K3/P6R/8 w - - 15 57"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kp/5r2/4K3/P6R/8 w - - 15 57"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kp/5r2/4K3/P6R/8 w - - 15 57", "move": "Rg2"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kp/5r2/4K3/P6R/8 w - - 15 57", "move": "Rxh5"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "8/5p2/4p3/4P1kR/5r2/4K3/P7/8 b - - 0 57", "move": "Kxh5"}}, {"to